The native decision runtime in crates/z-engine-decisions/src/providers/onnx/
(sequence.rs, decode.rs, runtime.rs, pyjson.rs) is a Rust port of Laya's
reference Python, release v0.3.22: the token sequence builder
(laya/common.py: serialize_state, render_options, build_sequence), the
answer decoding and temperatures (laya/onnx_agent.py: _encode_state,
_decode_answers, _infer_batch; laya/common.py: temp_bucket,
clamp_temperature, answer_confidence, collate_items). Changes: rewritten in
Rust; yes/no questions are sent as a two-option choice with neutral labels;
a score is reported from 0 to 1; option reordering, per-language
temperatures and usage statistics are left out. The test fixtures in
crates/z-engine-decisions/tests/fixtures/onnx/ were produced by running
Laya's own functions (generate.py there) and Laya's ONNXAgent on the
downloaded model (generate_answers.py there).

